    permits: "Connecticut enforces the Connecticut State Building Code (adopted from ICC) statewide. Every pool permit requires a signed application through the local building official, a zoning permit, an electrical permit, and a final health-department inspection in some towns. Barriers must be 48 inches minimum with self-closing/self-latching hardware; Connecticut also requires the pool to be separately fenced from the house where the house wall serves as part of the enclosure (more conservative than some states). Permit fees typically run $2,000–$3,200.",
